no, the full text shows none.\n\nHmm, alternatively the \"2005年\" could be testing retroactivity: if the rules were effective 2004-04-01, conduct in 2005 is covered. But if the exam is about whether the rules apply to older conduct... The mention of 2005 is just to establish it happened under the rules' validity.\n\nActually, you know what — maybe C is designed to be punishable via 13(9) (\"一年内连续出现2件以内错误公证文书的\" —1件 is within 2). The \"因个人的过失\" highlights that it's negligence, not intent (so 16(2)故意出具错误公证书 doesn't apply), and a single case → 严重警告 level. So C is punishable.\n\nSo the answer would be ABCD.\n\nHmm, let me double-check A once more. \"无正当理由，不接受某体育福利彩票中心对公证事项的委托\" — Hmm. Actually, wait. Consider:彩票开奖公证 — the lottery center commissions notarization of the lottery drawing. Is this \"指定的公益性公证事项\"? Under福利彩票管理办法, 开奖公证 must be notarized. It's a公益性 (public welfare) matter. In the textbook《公证与律师制度》, I believe there's discussion that公证员 must accept公益性的、指定的公证事项. The exam likely intends A as a violation (无正当理由拒绝接受公益性公证事项 → 警告).\n\nHmm, but the wording says \"委托\" not \"指定\". If the exam is testing precision, A might be the trap: refusing a委托 (ordinary entrustment) is not per se a violation because公证 is application-based and notaries can decline; only refusing \"指定的公益性公证事项\" violates12(1). But then \"体育福利彩票中心\" — is the委托 from a lottery center a \"指定\" matter? The lottery drawing notarization is usually organized by the 司法行政部门 and assigned to a notary office/notary (指定). Hmm.\n\nHmm, actually — wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the question comes from a specific exam with a published answer. Let me search the web more specifically.\n\nLet me try searching \"不接受某体育福利彩票中心\" on the web.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_72e942a4b6cf46fea543d578", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "\"体育福利彩票中心\" 公证员 \"不接受\" 惩戒"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_04a6610e42ee463e8cb3eb0f", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "公证